N:changelog-maintenance
D:Own release communication and change history. Use when documenting what changed, who is affected, and what migration or deprecation guidance must accompany a release.
G:changelog release-notes migration deprecation documentation
U[4]:
  Preparing a release note or changelog entry
  Communicating user-visible or operator-visible changes
  Documenting deprecations and removals
  Linking readers to the canonical migration path
S[5]{n,action}:
  1,Gather grounded change input from source owners
  2,Classify changes for readers
  3,Write impact-focused release communication
  4,Make deprecations and migrations actionable
  5,Keep the historical record trustworthy
R[4]:
  Do not redefine system behavior in the changelog
  Avoid vague summaries like miscellaneous fixes
  Include migration guidance for breaking changes
  Prefer reader impact over commit-log wording
